// The `operating-points` format, v1. A SCHEMA grammar, not a second TOML.
//
// The value terminals -- `string`, `boolean`, `float`, `integer`, `key`,
// `comment`, `sp`, `nl` -- come from `regimen/grammar.pest`, which the parser
// concatenates ahead of this file. One text says what a string is. A second
// copy of the TOML subset here would be the two-readers class at the terminal
// level, which this repository has already ruled on once.
//
// What this file adds is the shape the regimen grammar cannot say, and that
// shape is the whole reason operating points is a format rather than a
// regimen document:
//
//   * THE DOCUMENT IS ORDERED. The file's own rule is "matched by substring
//     against the served model id, IN FILE ORDER: the first table whose
//     `match` is a substring of the id wins", and it says why: `qwen3` is a
//     substring of `qwen3.6` and `qwen3.5`, so it comes after both. The
//     regimen projection is a table, and a table sorts. Run the real file
//     through it and it hands back gemma, qwen3, qwen3_5, qwen3_6 for a file
//     written qwen3_6, qwen3_5, qwen3, gemma -- inverted on the one axis the
//     rule depends on. Match `qwen3.6` against that and the `qwen3` entry
//     wins, with `thinking_kwarg = false`, while the entry that should have
//     won says true and carries the receipt "the /no_think soft switch is
//     DEAD on this model; the kwarg is the only working control". The wrong
//     answer reachable that way is the control that does not work.
//
//   * `nothink_ops` IS CLOSED, here, in the grammar. A closed vocabulary
//     checked after the parse is a vocabulary the parser accepted; checked
//     here, an unknown operation is not a document. These are the operations
//     measured safe to run with thinking suppressed, and everything not
//     listed keeps thinking -- so a typo that widened the list would suppress
//     thinking on an operation nobody measured.
//
//   * EVERY MODEL ENTRY CARRIES ITS SAMPLER AND ITS GATE. Both are required
//     and both are tables, because an entry missing one is an operating point
//     that does not say how the model was served, and the reason these are
//     transcribed measurements rather than preferences is that they say
//     exactly that.
//
// Not said here, and checked in Rust instead: that `[x.sampler]` belongs to
// the `[x]` above it. A back-reference across a header is not what a PEG is
// for, and the record format already puts its cross-row rules ("summary is
// the last row") in a structure check with a name. The same precedent, the
// same reason.

points_file = { SOI ~ ignorable* ~ model+ ~ ignorable* ~ EOI }

// Blank lines and whole-line comments, anywhere. The file opens with
// twenty-one lines of them and they are dogma too: the pinned digest covers
// the comments, so a grammar that could not read one could not read the file.
ignorable = _{ blank | comment_line }
comment_line = _{ sp* ~ comment ~ (nl | &EOI) }

// One model entry, in the order it was written.
model = { model_header ~ (ignorable | model_pair)* ~ sampler_table ~ ignorable* ~ gate_table ~ (ignorable | receipts_table)* }

model_header = { sp* ~ "[" ~ sp* ~ key ~ sp* ~ "]" ~ sp* ~ comment? ~ (nl | &EOI) }
sampler_table = { sp* ~ "[" ~ sp* ~ key ~ "." ~ sampler_name ~ sp* ~ "]" ~ sp* ~ comment? ~ (nl | &EOI) ~ (ignorable | plain_pair)* }
gate_table = { sp* ~ "[" ~ sp* ~ key ~ "." ~ gate_name ~ sp* ~ "]" ~ sp* ~ comment? ~ (nl | &EOI) ~ (ignorable | plain_pair)* }
receipts_table = { sp* ~ "[" ~ sp* ~ key ~ "." ~ receipts_name ~ sp* ~ "]" ~ sp* ~ comment? ~ (nl | &EOI) ~ (ignorable | plain_pair)* }
sampler_name = { "sampler" }
gate_name = { "gate" }
receipts_name = { "receipts" }

// The keys a model entry may carry, and nothing else. `match` and
// `nothink_ops` are required; the two thinking flags are not, because a model
// family that has no soft switch to describe should not have to say so.
model_pair = _{ match_pair | nothink_pair | thinking_kwarg_pair | preserve_thinking_pair }
match_pair = { sp* ~ "match" ~ sp* ~ "=" ~ sp* ~ string ~ sp* ~ comment? ~ (nl | &EOI) }
nothink_pair = { sp* ~ "nothink_ops" ~ sp* ~ "=" ~ sp* ~ nothink_array ~ sp* ~ comment? ~ (nl | &EOI) }
thinking_kwarg_pair = { sp* ~ "thinking_kwarg" ~ sp* ~ "=" ~ sp* ~ boolean ~ sp* ~ comment? ~ (nl | &EOI) }
preserve_thinking_pair = { sp* ~ "preserve_thinking" ~ sp* ~ "=" ~ sp* ~ boolean ~ sp* ~ comment? ~ (nl | &EOI) }

// The closed vocabulary. An empty list is admitted and means the same thing
// the file says it means: everything keeps thinking.
nothink_array = { "[" ~ sp* ~ (nothink_op ~ (sp* ~ "," ~ sp* ~ nothink_op)* ~ sp* ~ ","?)? ~ sp* ~ "]" }
nothink_op = { "\"extraction\"" | "\"judgment\"" | "\"audit\"" }

// Inside a sampler, a gate or a receipts table the keys are open -- a sampler
// setting is whatever the serving stack calls it, and a receipt is prose
// under a name the measurement chose. The VALUES are still the format's.
plain_pair = { sp* ~ key ~ sp* ~ "=" ~ sp* ~ plain_value ~ sp* ~ comment? ~ (nl | &EOI) }
plain_value = _{ string | boolean | float | integer }
